"""bench2: two benchmarks (triangle = CPU-heavy, cube = GPU-heavy), run INSIDE the DroidDeck guest (Linux arm64 glibc under proot, like a game),
comparing our mali-open ICD with the Mali bridge (the guest's default libvulkan.so.1).

  tools/bench2 <alias|class> [--driver ours|bridge|both] [--bench triangle|cube|all] [--reps 5] [--secs 8] [--sweep] [--dry-run]
  tools/bench2 --report            regenerate bench/RESULTS.md from bench/results.jsonl
  tools/bench2 --list              print the planned runs

<alias|class> = farm alias (cmf, poco-x8, poco-x4) or class (v10, v11, v13) from ~/.config/mali-farm/devices.toml.
Per phone: qsafe lock (/tmp/qsafe-<lock>.lock, non-blocking: busy = pending, never retried in a loop), owner disable switch, health gate
(battery 20/50 %, 43/38 C), focus rule (launcher/settings only), farm adb routing. Appends one row per (phone, driver, version, benchmark,
variant) to bench/results.jsonl, then regenerates bench/RESULTS.md. Nothing is installed on the phone (files go to Download/ and /tmp in the guest).

Workloads (bench/mdbench, one binary, Vulkan + Wayland WSI through the guest compositor, started via `reaper SteamLaunch AppId=769`):
  triangle: scene drawcalls, 20000 draws/frame, ONE triangle per draw, dynamic-UBO descriptor offset per draw (driver CPU overhead dominates)
  cube    : scene cube + 8 overdraw layers + 24-iteration ALU fragment shader, depth on, 1280x720 (and native screen size)
  each both presented (wayland) and offscreen (headless, no 120 Hz cap). Headline metrics: CPU ms/frame (record+submit) and GPU ms/frame (timestamps).
"""
